<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>11 · AROUND — 环绕旋转、漫无目的闲逛、规避与苏醒<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.10</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>AROUND: Circular Path, Aimlessness, Circumvention & Recovery</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>72</b> 个独立义项 • <b>216</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 10 (Around/Round, by, past: Over, all around, all over, all across, about)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>半圆/全圆环绕路径 (Fig. 10.1)、绕轴自转与非线性漫游 (Fig. 10.5)</b>：AROUND（英式常作 ROUND）是一个仅约 400 年历史的年轻介词（莎士比亚与钦定版圣经中尚未出现，当时用 ABOUT）。正因为它的轨迹是弯曲或画圈的，天然排斥“笔直奔向目标的急迫感”。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>Many students waste time fooling around. / Tired of waiting around for people who didn't show up?</i> [Ch.10 (8)-(9)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>Lo and behold, he finally came around to my way of thinking.</i> (态度旋转 180° 转变过来) [Ch.10 (12)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>AROUND vs STRAIGHT / ABOUT (Ch.10 §2.7 Fig.10.5)</b>：因为路径不走直线，AROUND 成为表达<b>漫无目的、闲散、拖延或瞎混</b>的最佳小品词（<i>wander/fool/wait/lounge around</i>），比 ABOUT 更强调悠闲不紧迫；<i>get around to doing</i> 因“绕弯路不走捷径”而转喻“拖延很久才抽出时间做”。</li><li><b>绕过障碍 vs 翻越障碍 (Ch.10 §2.8 Fig.10.6)</b>：<i>get over a problem</i> 是从上方翻越困难，而 <i>get around a problem/regulation</i> 是从侧面画弧线绕开规避。</li><li><b>Spin/Turn around vs Roll over (Ch.10 §2.5)</b>：AROUND 的隐含参照物是垂直自转轴（在水平面上转身或改变心意 <i>come around to my way of thinking</i>），而 OVER 是绕水平重心轴上下翻转。</li></ul></div></div></details>

